ted the country in international matches, solidifying his status as a citizen of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland.\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1161, "end": 1214, "text": "Fulton's cricketing achievements are well-documented."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1215, "end": 1297, "text": "He played 144 first-class matches, scoring over 4,500 runs and taking 234 wickets."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1298, "end": 1440, "text": "His impressive record earned him a place in the prestigious Marylebone Cricket Club (MCC), the governing body of cricket in England and Wales."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1441, "end": 1604, "text": "Data from the UK Census of 1901, which was conducted during Fulton's playing career, lists him as a resident of England, further supporting his citizenship status."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1605, "end": 1762, "text": "The census records provide a snapshot of the population at the time, offering valuable insights into the demographics of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1763, "end": 1928, "text": "In an interview, cricket historian and author, Stephen Wagg, noted, \"Herbert Fulton's life and career are inextricably linked to the UK of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1929, "end": 2051, "text": "His contributions to English cricket are a testament to his citizenship and his place in the country's sporting heritage.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2052, "end": 2199, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence overwhelmingly supports the claim that Herbert Fulton was a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2200, "end": 2383, "text": "Through his cricketing achievements, historical 